From 2537b27607d4e7e780aaaa57faefe3365f1e4666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrin Jalali <adrin.jalali@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:34:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gh-152235: Also track sets built from a large container
 at its position

On top of tracking sets filled from an iterator at a reserved position: a
set built from a list, tuple, dict, set or frozenset with 1024 or more
elements is tracked right after that container in the GC list.  The
container was usually tracked ahead of the elements it holds, so the set
stays ahead of them when it becomes their only owner (s = set(big_list);
del big_list), and full collections don't scatter them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
